@attribute [Route($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Frameworks}/{GlobalValues.Framework_Path_Part_Modal}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Accessibility}")]

<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.Framework_Name_Modal @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Accessibility</PageTitle>

<h1>@GlobalValues.Framework_Name_Modal @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Accessibility</h1>
<p>
    The Modal Dialog was built using the HTML Dialog API and follows all best practices for modal dialogs. As the framework uses the native HTML Dialog, when open, all
    content behind its backdrop is effectively made inert, disallowing any user the ability to navigate to, or interact with that content whilst the dialog remains open.
</p>
<p>
    <strong>Note:</strong>As the escape key mechanism has been overriden, if the user cancels any dialog via the escape key then the focus must be returned to the triggering element.
</p>
<h2 id="dialog-keyboard">Keyboard interaction</h2>
<ul aria-labelledby="dialog-keyboard">
    <li>
        <kbd class="@Kbd.Base @Kbd.Scheme(KbdScheme.Neutral)">Escape</kbd> - closes the top most dialog if a handler has not been specified. If one has been specified then you control whether or not the dialog should close,
        as this could be a popup form with unsaved changes, and you may want to get confirmation from the user first etc.
        <br /><strong>Note: </strong> If the Announcement History popover (non-modal dialog) is open, then the escape key will close that first.
        .
    </li>
</ul>

<h2 id="device-testing">Accessibility device testing</h2>

<ul aria-labelledby="device-testing">
    <li>JAWS, Narrator and NVDA on Windows were each paired with every one of the following browsers: Google Chrome, Microsoft Edge and Mozilla Firefox.</li>
    <li>VoiceOver on macOS was paired with Apple's Safari.</li>
    <li>VoiceOver on iPhone was paired with mobile Safari.</li>
    <li>Talkback on Android was paired with mobile Google Chrome.</li>
    <li>Voice access on Windows 11</li>
</ul>

<p>
    <strong>Note: </strong> Testing was performed with the latest browser and assistive technologies versions that were available at the time of testing (see release history on the installation page for approximate testing dates)
</p>


<h2 id="screen-reader-quirks">Screen reader quirks or known issues</h2>
<ul aria-labelledby="screen-reader-quirks">
    <li>
        <p>
            <b>Safari browser.</b> Safari has, at the time of writing multiple issues regarding using a popover inside of nested modal dialogs and from my investigations, reordering issues of nested modal dialogs.
        </p>
        <p>
            What does this mean, there is an edge case that I cannot do anything about. Lets say you open a dialog and then launch another dialog, everything will work perfectly.
            Lets say now in the second nested dialog (it works fine in a single dialog), you open a popover (non-modal dialog) such as the Announcement History component. At this point it all works fine, and
            if you use the buttons to close the popover, its OK. But if you use the escape key, the popover will close but then Safari puts the dialogs in the wrong order. You then tab and the ordering is
            restored.
        </p>
        <p>
            <strong>Note:</strong> All other browsers that I tested worked perfectly without issue, it was only this one edge case when using Safari on macOS (iPhone was not effected given its touch the buttons) I came across when
            testing. I will from time to time check up on this, but I cannot control how safari orders the top layer items.
        </p>
    </li>
</ul>

<div class="flex-content justify-content-between">
    <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Button_Class @GlobalValues.Link_Button_Left_Arrow_Modifier" href="@($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Frameworks}/{GlobalValues.Framework_Path_Part_Modal}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Installation}")">
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>@GlobalValues.Framework_Name_Modal - @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Installation</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </a>
    <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Button_Class @GlobalValues.Link_Button_Right_Arrow_Modifier" href="@($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Frameworks}/{GlobalValues.Framework_Path_Part_Modal}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Api}")">
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>@GlobalValues.Framework_Name_Modal - @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Api</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </a>
</div>
